{
  "item": {
    "id": "b8a1e50e-1ef9-425d-b3d1-4e1b3cb6368f",
    "content_type": "generic",
    "workflow_state": "public",
    "page_title": "Transforming events in flight",
    "short_description": "Reshape, filter, and enrich events as they pass through a pipeline.",
    "body": "<h1>Transforming events in flight</h1>
<p>Transforms are intermediate processing steps applied to <a href="{{cms:item/6277e4fb-3e99-45b0-a7f6-aefe69c5778f}}">events</a> as they travel between a source connector and a destination in a <a href="{{cms:item/5ac66235-69dc-4092-b430-9d68837e0c76}}">pipeline</a>. You can use transforms to reshape payload structures, filter out unwanted records, and enrich events with additional context.</p>

<h2>1. Reshaping events</h2>
<p>Use reshape transforms to rename fields, restructure nested objects, or strip sensitive and unneeded keys before writing to downstream storage.</p>

{{ds:component/code-block|filename=reshape-transform.json|language=json|code=&#123;
  "type": "reshape",
  "config": &#123;
    "rename": &#123;
      "customer_email": "email",
      "amt_cents": "amount_cents"
    &#125;,
    "drop": ["internal_notes", "raw_ip"]
  &#125;
&#125;}}

<h2>2. Filtering events</h2>
<p>Filtering lets you conditionally route or drop events based on payload criteria. Non-matching events are discarded immediately, saving destination throughput and storage.</p>

{{ds:component/code-block|filename=filter-transform.json|language=json|code=&#123;
  "type": "filter",
  "config": &#123;
    "condition": "payload.status == 'completed' && payload.amount_cents > 0"
  &#125;
&#125;}}

{{ds:component/alert|variant=info|title=Dropped events|body_html=<p>Filtered-out events do not trigger retries or dead-letter queue entries; they are treated as successfully skipped.</p>}}

<h2>3. Enriching events</h2>
<p>Enrichment transforms add metadata, computed values, or static contextual fields to the event payload before delivery.</p>

{{ds:component/code-block|filename=enrich-transform.json|language=json|code=&#123;
  "type": "enrich",
  "config": &#123;
    "add_fields": &#123;
      "environment": "production",
      "processed_by": "godzilla-pipeline-v2"
    &#125;
  &#125;
&#125;}}

<h2>Configuring transforms in a pipeline</h2>
<p>Transforms are supplied as an ordered array on the pipeline definition. Godzilla executes each transform sequentially for every event.</p>

{{ds:component/code-block|filename=pipeline-with-transforms.json|language=json|code=&#123;
  "name": "orders-with-transforms",
  "source_connector_id": "conn_pg_orders",
  "destination_connector_id": "conn_snowflake_dw",
  "transforms": [
    &#123;
      "type": "filter",
      "config": &#123; "condition": "payload.amount_cents > 0" &#125;
    &#125;,
    &#123;
      "type": "reshape",
      "config": &#123; "drop": ["raw_ip"] &#125;
    &#125;,
    &#123;
      "type": "enrich",
      "config": &#123; "add_fields": &#123; "region": "us-east" &#125; &#125;
    &#125;
  ]
&#125;}}

{{ds:component/alert|variant=warning|title=Order of execution matters|body_html=<p>Because transforms run sequentially, placing filter steps first avoids unnecessary processing on events that will ultimately be dropped.</p>}}

<h2>Next steps</h2>
<p>Learn how Godzilla deals with transformation and destination write failures in <a href="{{cms:item/062cc815-2b65-45b1-b36c-6ea67dfd1a0c}}">Handling errors & retries</a>, or manage your pipelines directly using the <a href="{{cms:item/0db56c61-3928-4b78-b0bd-e59febe8ed72}}">Pipelines endpoint</a>.</p>

{{ds:component/docs-pagination|prev_href={{cms:item/3448ffab-598c-46e7-bda6-e7cdc4a1e7c6}}|prev_label=Connecting a data source|next_href={{cms:item/062cc815-2b65-45b1-b36c-6ea67dfd1a0c}}|next_label=Handling errors & retries}}",
